src/ is a single state machine (useAuthSession's status: loading|loggedOut|mustChangePassword|ready) rendered by App.tsx, with three feature groups underneath: features/auth/ (public flows — SignupPage, LoginPage, ForgotPasswordPage, and ForcedChangePage which App.tsx shows instead of everything else while mustChangePassword is set — a UX-only mirror of auth-server's own server-side allowlist, which enforces this regardless), features/account/ (AccountPage: change-password, add/verify email — auto-verifies on mount when landing on /verify-email?token=..., rotate-master behind a window.confirm), and features/keys/ (KeysPage: list/create/rotate/revoke API keys with the show-once token box, structurally mirroring mud-builder-client's AccessPage key panel). api/client.ts is the one place that knows auth-server's endpoint shapes (cross-checked directly against apps/auth-server/src/routes/*.ts rather than trusting docs/auth-server.md alone) and always sets credentials:'include'. App.css holds every auc-* class (never mud-builder's mb-* classes — separate namespace, mirrored layout idiom only).
